      "payload": {
        "result": {
          "source": "github",
          "title": "Discussion: replace post-hoc compact-changelog with file-per-change tooling (evaluate changie for 2026)",
          "url": "https://github.com/genealogix/glx/issues/858",
          "reactions": 0,
          "comments": 2,
          "author": "isaacschepp",
          "created_at": "2026-05-15T18:41:08Z",
          "body_snippet": "## Summary\n\n`compact-changelog.md` exists because agentic edits create duplicate `### Added` sections, self-cancelling Added/Removed pairs, and follow-up Fixed entries that should fold into the original Added. **File-per-change tools eliminate this class of problem at the source by writing each change to its own file**, then assembling at release time. The compact-changelog command is, at best, post-hoc cleanup of a problem that need not exist.\n\nThis is a Discussion, not a Bug or Enhancement \u2014 i"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "scanner": "failures",
